     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Hi D-RUG,</div><div><br></div><div>Following up on a great presentation by Will Hemstrom today on writing packages in R, here is a community call for rOpenSci on testing from Stefanie Butland, the rOpenSci Community Manager.</div><div><br></div><div><h4 style=\"margin:0px 0px 10px;line-height:1.2;font-size:15px;color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial\">All are welcome to join rOpenSci&#39;s Community Call on testing in R package development<br></h4><div>Thursday, December 5th, 2019; no RSVP needed. 2 speakers &amp; 20 mins for Q&amp;A<br></div><p style=\"font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial\"><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34)\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Event Details:<span> </span><a href=\"https://ropensci.org/blog/2019/11/12/commcall-dec2019/\" style=\"background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-color:transparent;color:rgb(0,136,204);text-decoration-line:none;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://ropensci.org/blog/2019/11/12/commcall-dec2019/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792465605379000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0bg8AQZy6o6K9Py7sWg6Rw\">https://ropensci.org/blog/2019/11/12/commcall-dec2019/</a><br>Tweet to share:<span> </span><a href=\"https://twitter.com/rOpenSci/status/1194646101736882182\" style=\"background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-color:transparent;color:rgb(0,136,204);text-decoration-line:none;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://twitter.com/rOpenSci/status/1194646101736882182&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792465605379000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1WRo37UiE0vrL_kplTFGaE\">https://twitter.com/rOpenSci/status/1194646101736882182</a></span></span></span></span></p><p style=\"font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial\"><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34)\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Description</span></span></span></span><br></p><div><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34)\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">As someone with a background in science, not software engineering, <b>Steffi LaZerte</b>\r\n will share her experiences using automated testing in R to ensure that \r\npackages do what they’re supposed to do, on all the operating systems \r\nthey’re supposed to do it on, and that they handle weird stuff \r\ngracefully.</span></span></span></span><br></div><p style=\"font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial\"><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34)\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><b>Rich FitzJohn</b><span> </span>will\r\n talk about how to make testing much more useful than a chore that one \r\ndoes just because it is “best practice”, focussing on how testing has \r\nbeen useful in his work - refactoring code bases, preventing \r\nregressions, and improving how code is written in the first place. He \r\nwill discuss how testing can help at the heart of processes, \r\nparticularly in collaborative work, and how automating your testing \r\nleaves you with more time and energy to focus on your software, and \r\ndescribe strategies for testing as systems grow more complex, such as \r\nusing mocking to simulate components.</span></span></span></span><br></p><p style=\"font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial\"><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34)\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Speaker bios, how to join the call: </span></span></span></span><a href=\"https://ropensci.org/blog/2019/11/12/commcall-dec2019/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://ropensci.org/blog/2019/11/12/commcall-dec2019/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792465605379000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0bg8AQZy6o6K9Py7sWg6Rw\">https://ropensci.org/blog/2019/11/12/commcall-dec2019/</a><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34)\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">.</span></span></span></span></p><p style=\"font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial\"><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34)\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">What’s your story?</span></span></span></span><br></p><ul style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px 0px 0px 40px;clear:both;color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial\"><li>What motivated you to start testing?<br></li><li>What do you wish your past-self knew?<br></li><li>What are your favorite resources on the topic?<br></li><li>What questions do you have?<br></li></ul><p style=\"font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial\"><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34)\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif\">Tell us in the <a href=\"https://discuss.ropensci.org/t/community-call-on-testing-dec-5-2019-tell-us-what-you-wish-your-past-self-knew/1877\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://discuss.ropensci.org/t/community-call-on-testing-dec-5-2019-tell-us-what-you-wish-your-past-self-knew/1877&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792465605379000&amp;usg=AOvVaw148yz6Y0k563SZzNuEXIS0\">pre-Call discussion</a></span></span></span></span></p><p style=\"font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial\"><br></p><p style=\"font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial\">Best,</p><p style=\"font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial\">Taylor<br></p></div>-- <br><div dir=\"ltr\" data-smartmail=\"gmail_signature\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Taylor Reiter</div><div>PhD Candidate<br></div><div>Food Science Graduate Group</div><div>Lab for Data Intensive Biology</div>University of California, Davis</div></div></div></div></div>\r\n"
